DEBUG ONLY -- NOT PART OF ANY BUILD.

Progress markers through tcc_new, so a segfault says WHICH STATEMENT.

    M50  reached the field writes
    M51  s->ppfp = stdout survived
    M52  s->include_stack_ptr = s->include_stack survived
    M53  tcc_set_lib_path survived, so tcc_new is complete

The LAST marker printed is the last statement that survived; the fault is in
whatever follows it.

THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS PATCH USED EXIT SYSCALLS AND WAS USELESS. An exit
marker ends the process, so only the first could ever fire, and its code said
nothing beyond "the function was entered" -- which the ladder had already
established. It reported "FAULTS AT: s->ppfp = stdout" purely because that is
where the first marker sat.

write(2, ...) is M2libc's syscall wrapper, which the ladder proved works at
rung A2, and it does not disturb control flow.

--- a/libtcc.c
+++ b/libtcc.c
@@ -908,11 +908,15 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_NEW_DTAGS
     s->enable_new_dtags = 1;
 #endif
+    write(2, "M50\n", 4);
     s->ppfp = stdout;
+    write(2, "M51\n", 4);
     /* might be used in error() before preprocess_start() */
     s->include_stack_ptr = s->include_stack;
+    write(2, "M52\n", 4);
 
     tcc_set_lib_path(s, CONFIG_TCCDIR);
+    write(2, "M53\n", 4);
 #ifdef CONFIG_TCC_SWITCHES /* predefined options */
     tcc_set_options(s, CONFIG_TCC_SWITCHES);
 #endif
